{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Living the Dream", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "I Did It!", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 16, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe ways of solving problems and getting things done in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Causative<span class=\"italic\"> Get </span>and <span class=\"italic\">Have</span>", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We use a causative verb when we want to talk about something that someone else did for us. It means that the subject caused the action to happen, but didn't do it themselves. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the causative verbs <span class=\"italic\">get/have </span> when you want to make it clear that the subject paid, asked, or persuaded the other person to do something. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Sometimes, you use <span class=\"italic\">get </span> when you want to convey the feeling that you need to convince someone to do something. <span class=\"italic\">Have </span> is a little more neutral.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "My last supervisor got her editors to be extremely precise.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "My colleague had the two of us take a seminar in time management", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'll only get you to answer two more questions. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I think I got you to answer everything. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Get\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" [get + person + to + verb]\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">My boss <span class=\\\"strong\\\">got her to work</span>  late on Tuesday.<br> Did the boss <span class=\\\"strong\\\">get you to work </span> on Saturday?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to convince to do something or to trick someone into doing something\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"[get + object + past participle]\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">got my jacket cleaned</span> before the meeting. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"more informal way of saying that someone else did something for you (it focuses on object not the subject)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"[have + object + verb]\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Dr. Smith <span class=\\\"strong\\\">had his nurse take</span>  the patient's temperature.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to give someone the responsibility to do something\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" [have + person + verb]\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">had the hairdresser style</span> my hair for me. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to give someone the responsibility to do something on your behalf\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " What-Clauses and Long Noun Phrases as Subjects", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " <span class=\"strong\">What-clauses </span> are used to help us focus on a particular part of the sentence and to emphasise what we want to say by introducing it as a relative clause.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">What-clauses</span> are usually linked to the clause that we want to focus on with <span class=\"strong\">is </span> or <span class=\"strong\">was</span> .", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Compare: <br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What</span>  I now need <span class=\"strong\">is</span>  a new car.</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">A new car is <span class=\"strong\">what I </span> now need.</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What</span>  I enjoyed most <span class=\"strong\">was </span> seeing their new office.</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Seeing their new office <span class=\"strong\">was what </span> I enjoyed most.</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">What-clauses </span> </span> are often used with verbs like <span class=\"strong\">adore</span>, <span class=\"strong\">dislike</span>, <span class=\"strong\">enjoy</span>,  <span class=\"strong\">hate</span>, <span class=\"strong\">like</span>, <span class=\"strong\">loathe</span>, <span class=\"strong\"> love</span>, <span class=\"strong\">need</span>, <span class=\"strong\">prefer</span>, <span class=\"strong\">want</span>.</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Compare:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What </span> I enjoyed most <span class=\"strong\">was </span> seeing their new office.</span> <br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Seeing their new office <span class=\"strong\">was what </span> I enjoyed most.</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": " <span class=\"strong\">What-clauses </span>are also often used with <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">does</span>/<span class=\"strong\">do</span>/<span class=\"strong\">did </span> </span>and </span> when we want to give emphasis to the whole sentence, rather than a particular clause.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Compare: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">The manager interviewed all the salespeople first.</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What </span> the manager <span class=\"strong\">did </span> first <span class=\"strong\">was </span> interview all the salespeople </span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "These sentences are useful in writing where we cannot use intonation for emphasis, but they are also often used in speech.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What we do here is often very stressful.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "What I want is a job that is tailored to my competencies and which includes writing and editing. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "What I think is my greatest strength is my writing skills. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "imminent", "type": "name"}, {"content": "happening very soon", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The website says the launch of several new books is imminent. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when you negotiate a salary.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "attention to detail", "type": "name"}, {"content": "noticing small, specific things", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I have strong attention to detail when it comes to my writing.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "thrive", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to do well", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I thrived under quick deadlines and multiple projects. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "launch", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to start up", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The website says the launch of several new books is imminent. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "salary", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a fixed regular payment for work", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: What are your salary expectations? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "With a partner, create a job you need to fill.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a list of all the skills you want applicants to have.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Include descriptions of job duties using passive modals to explain.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a list of questions you would like to ask.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You will interview various classmates for the position.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "One of you will ask the questions, the other person will take note of the subject's body language.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Afterwards, give feedback on how the subject did.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Interview the next candidate and switch roles with your partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I make a list of skills needed for a particular job listing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use passive modals to explain job duties.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I practice interviewing questions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I analyze body language.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give feedback on how to interview for a job.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0